SUMMARY:What Has Become Available Recently (Past 15-25 Years) in Various Old and New Archives That Will Enable Us to Write New Histories of Modern South Asia?
DESCRIPTION:27 November 2026/११ मङ्सिर २०८३ (शुक्रबार\, दिउँसो ४ बजे)\nOpen Panel: Public Session\n\nWhat Has Become Available Recently (Past 15-25 Years) in Various Old and New Archives That Will Enable Us to Write New Histories of Modern South Asia?\n&amp\;nbsp\;\nPanelists:\nProjit Bihari Mukharji\, Dean and Professor\, TCG-CREST\, Kolkata and Professor in History\, Ashoka University\, India\nAjapa Sharma\, Historian\, Martin Chautari\nGaurav C. Garg\, Assistant Professor in History\, Ashoka University\, India\n\n\nModerator:\nPratyoush Onta\, Historian\, Martin Chautari\n\n&amp\;nbsp\;\n\nThis is a public event and participation is open to all.\nhttps://martinchautari.org.np/events/what-has-become-available-recently-past-15-25-years-in-various-old-and-new-archives-that-will-enable-us-to-write-new-histories-of-modern-south-asia
URL:https://martinchautari.org.np/events/what-has-become-available-recently-past-15-25-years-in-various-old-and-new-archives-that-will-enable-us-to-write-new-histories-of-modern-south-asia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
